              "titleEn": "CPI decomposition: principles and architecture",
              "objective": "以「CPI 分解」建立可檢查的架構、原理與驗證依據。",
              "objectiveEn": "Establish reviewable architecture, principles and evidence for cpi decomposition.",
              "instruction": "先觀看師傅示意，辨識「CPI 分解」的資料、控制與時間關係。重疊停頓不能直接重複相加。 在離線工作臺畫出元件／資料流，列出輸入、輸出、保存狀態與合法轉移；建立基準與擾動兩種假想情境，寫下可被反駁的預測。以「用本課非重疊假設核算。」設計下一步驗證。記錄版本、單位、未知參數與模型外的行為。",
              "instructionEn": "Watch the mentor and identify data, control and timing relationships for cpi decomposition. Overlapping stalls cannot simply be added twice. Draw components/data flows offline; specify inputs, outputs, retained state and legal transitions. Build baseline and perturbed hypothetical cases and make a falsifiable prediction. Plan validation using: Audit the course nonoverlap assumption. Record versions, units, unknowns and out-of-model behavior.",
              "observation": "用本課非重疊假設核算。",
              "observationEn": "Audit the course nonoverlap assumption.",
              "failure": "常見誤判：寬解碼保證所有程式 CPI 同比下降。 本步需分開功能正確、資源上界與證據範圍，不可把假想結果當作真實平臺保證。",
              "failureEn": "Common mistake: Wider decode guarantees proportional CPI reduction. Separate correctness, resource bounds and evidence scope; hypothetical results are not real-platform guarantees.",
              "check": "提交「CPI 分解」的兩情境架構／狀態圖、參數表與可反駁預測；標出哪些資料支援「重疊停頓不能直接重複相加。」。",
              "checkEn": "Submit cpi decomposition two-case architecture/state diagrams, parameter table and falsifiable prediction; identify evidence supporting the principle.",
              "knowledge": [
                {
                  "id": "a302-v11-27-k1",
                  "title": "CPI 分解的原理與邊界",
                  "titleEn": "CPI decomposition principle and boundaries",
                  "text": "重疊停頓不能直接重複相加。",
                  "textEn": "Overlapping stalls cannot simply be added twice.",
                  "sourceIds": [
