              "objective": "以「編譯映射」建立可檢查的架構、原理與驗證依據。",
              "objectiveEn": "Establish reviewable architecture, principles and evidence for compiler mapping.",
              "instruction": "先觀看師傅示意，辨識「編譯映射」的資料、控制與時間關係。融合可減少交通但增加局部資源。 在離線工作臺畫出元件／資料流，列出輸入、輸出、保存狀態與合法轉移；建立基準與擾動兩種假想情境，寫下可被反駁的預測。以「比較融合前後暫存量。」設計下一步驗證。記錄版本、單位、未知參數與模型外的行為。",
              "instructionEn": "Watch the mentor and identify data, control and timing relationships for compiler mapping. Fusion saves traffic but consumes local resources. Draw components/data flows offline; specify inputs, outputs, retained state and legal transitions. Build baseline and perturbed hypothetical cases and make a falsifiable prediction. Plan validation using: Compare temporary storage before and after fusion. Record versions, units, unknowns and out-of-model behavior.",
              "observation": "比較融合前後暫存量。",
              "observationEn": "Compare temporary storage before and after fusion.",
              "failure": "常見誤判：BF16 與 FP16 有相同指數和尾數配置。 本步需分開功能正確、資源上界與證據範圍，不可把假想結果當作真實平臺保證。",
              "failureEn": "Common mistake: BF16 and FP16 have identical exponent and mantissa layouts. Separate correctness, resource bounds and evidence scope; hypothetical results are not real-platform guarantees.",
              "check": "提交「編譯映射」的兩情境架構／狀態圖、參數表與可反駁預測；標出哪些資料支援「融合可減少交通但增加局部資源。」。",
              "checkEn": "Submit compiler mapping two-case architecture/state diagrams, parameter table and falsifiable prediction; identify evidence supporting the principle.",
              "knowledge": [
                {
                  "id": "a305-v11-25-k1",
                  "title": "編譯映射的原理與邊界",
                  "titleEn": "Compiler mapping principle and boundaries",
                  "text": "融合可減少交通但增加局部資源。",
                  "textEn": "Fusion saves traffic but consumes local resources.",
                  "sourceIds": [
                    "v11a-tpu",
                    "v11a-bf16"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "a305-v11-25-k2",
                  "title": "編譯映射的驗證設計",
                  "titleEn": "Compiler mapping validation design",
                  "text": "比較融合前後暫存量。 保留基準與擾動的完整輸入／輸出，以語義、容量或時間條件檢查，並明列假想模型未涵蓋的現實因素。",
                  "textEn": "Compare temporary storage before and after fusion. Retain complete inputs/outputs for baseline and perturbation, check semantic/capacity/timing criteria and state real-world factors omitted from the hypothetical model.",
                  "sourceIds": [
                    "v11a-tpu",
                    "v11a-bf16"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "quiz": {
                "question": "本步審查「編譯映射」與整體「張量運算加速器」時，哪項陳述或驗證有依據？",
                "questionEn": "When reviewing compiler mapping within tensor-compute accelerators, which statement or check is supported?",
                "options": [
                  "融合可減少交通但增加局部資源。",
                  "BF16 與 FP16 有相同指數和尾數配置。",
                  "峰值 FLOP/s 可直接當作端到端訓練吞吐。"
                ],
                "optionsEn": [
                  "Fusion saves traffic but consumes local resources.",
                  "BF16 and FP16 have identical exponent and mantissa layouts.",
                  "Peak FLOP/s equals end-to-end training throughput."
                ],
                "answer": 0,
                "explanation": "融合可減少交通但增加局部資源。 比較融合前後暫存量。 其餘選項混淆不同架構或證據的適用邊界。",
                "explanationEn": "Fusion saves traffic but consumes local resources. Compare temporary storage before and after fusion. The alternatives confuse architectural or evidence boundaries."
              }
