              "objectiveEn": "Establish reviewable architecture, principles and evidence for virtual channels.",
              "instruction": "先觀看師傅示意，辨識「虛擬通道」的資料、控制與時間關係。共用實體鏈路可分離等待佇列。 在離線工作臺畫出元件／資料流，列出輸入、輸出、保存狀態與合法轉移；建立基準與擾動兩種假想情境，寫下可被反駁的預測。以「比較阻塞前後的隊列。」設計下一步驗證。記錄版本、單位、未知參數與模型外的行為。",
              "instructionEn": "Watch the mentor and identify data, control and timing relationships for virtual channels. Virtual channels separate queues on shared links. Draw components/data flows offline; specify inputs, outputs, retained state and legal transitions. Build baseline and perturbed hypothetical cases and make a falsifiable prediction. Plan validation using: Compare queues with and without blockage. Record versions, units, unknowns and out-of-model behavior.",
              "observation": "比較阻塞前後的隊列。",
              "observationEn": "Compare queues with and without blockage.",
              "failure": "常見誤判：增加虛擬通道即自動證明無死鎖。 本步需分開功能正確、資源上界與證據範圍，不可把假想結果當作真實平臺保證。",
              "failureEn": "Common mistake: More virtual channels automatically prove deadlock freedom. Separate correctness, resource bounds and evidence scope; hypothetical results are not real-platform guarantees.",
              "check": "提交「虛擬通道」的兩情境架構／狀態圖、參數表與可反駁預測；標出哪些資料支援「共用實體鏈路可分離等待佇列。」。",
              "checkEn": "Submit virtual channels two-case architecture/state diagrams, parameter table and falsifiable prediction; identify evidence supporting the principle.",
              "knowledge": [
                {
                  "id": "a307-v11-17-k1",
                  "title": "虛擬通道的原理與邊界",
                  "titleEn": "Virtual channels principle and boundaries",
                  "text": "共用實體鏈路可分離等待佇列。",
                  "textEn": "Virtual channels separate queues on shared links.",
                  "sourceIds": [
