                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "a307-v11-17-k2",
                  "title": "虛擬通道的驗證設計",
                  "titleEn": "Virtual channels validation design",
                  "text": "比較阻塞前後的隊列。 保留基準與擾動的完整輸入／輸出，以語義、容量或時間條件檢查，並明列假想模型未涵蓋的現實因素。",
                  "textEn": "Compare queues with and without blockage. Retain complete inputs/outputs for baseline and perturbation, check semantic/capacity/timing criteria and state real-world factors omitted from the hypothetical model.",
                  "sourceIds": [
                    "v11a-noc",
                    "v11a-garnet"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "quiz": {
                "question": "本步審查「虛擬通道」與整體「片上網路路由器」時，哪項陳述或驗證有依據？",
                "questionEn": "When reviewing virtual channels within network-on-chip routers, which statement or check is supported?",
                "options": [
                  "增加虛擬通道即自動證明無死鎖。",
                  "共用實體鏈路可分離等待佇列。",
                  "鏈路峰值可直接當作全部端點吞吐。"
                ],
                "optionsEn": [
                  "More virtual channels automatically prove deadlock freedom.",
                  "Virtual channels separate queues on shared links.",
                  "Peak link rate equals total endpoint throughput."
                ],
                "answer": 1,
                "explanation": "共用實體鏈路可分離等待佇列。 比較阻塞前後的隊列。 其餘選項混淆不同架構或證據的適用邊界。",
                "explanationEn": "Virtual channels separate queues on shared links. Compare queues with and without blockage. The alternatives confuse architectural or evidence boundaries."
              }
