              "titleEn": "Timer resolution: experiment and validation",
              "objective": "用「比較 tick 與高解析計時。」檢查「計時器精度」的假設、結果及失效邊界。",
              "objectiveEn": "Validate assumptions, outcomes and failure boundaries for timer resolution using the specified experiment.",
              "instruction": "重播師傅對「計時器精度」的示範，在自己的隔離模型或試算表執行：比較 tick 與高解析計時。 核對「時鐘量化誤差需列入 deadline 裕量。」是否成立；保留輸入、預期、實際結果與差異。至少提出兩個競爭原因，選擇一項能區分它們的新增觀察。依事前定義的語義、容量或延遲條件判斷通過／保留，未執行的真實平臺項目不得標為實測。",
              "instructionEn": "Replay the mentor for timer resolution and execute in your own isolated model or worksheet: Compare tick and high-resolution timing. Check the principle: Clock quantization belongs in deadline margins. Preserve input, expected output, observed output and differences. Propose two competing causes and a discriminating observation. Apply predefined semantic, capacity or latency criteria and mark untested real-platform claims unresolved.",
              "observation": "比較 tick 與高解析計時。",
              "observationEn": "Compare tick and high-resolution timing.",
              "failure": "常見誤判：平均延遲合格即證明硬即時合格。 本步需分開功能正確、資源上界與證據範圍，不可把假想結果當作真實平臺保證。",
              "failureEn": "Common mistake: Passing mean latency proves hard real-time compliance. Separate correctness, resource bounds and evidence scope; hypothetical results are not real-platform guarantees.",
              "check": "提交「計時器精度」的輸入與結果對照、競爭原因、接受／保留理由；逐項說明「比較 tick 與高解析計時。」的證據與尚未驗證範圍。",
              "checkEn": "Submit timer resolution input/output comparisons, competing causes and pass/hold rationale; state evidence and untested scope for the experiment.",
              "knowledge": [
                {
                  "id": "a309-v11-24-k1",
                  "title": "計時器精度的原理與邊界",
                  "titleEn": "Timer resolution principle and boundaries",
                  "text": "時鐘量化誤差需列入 deadline 裕量。",
                  "textEn": "Clock quantization belongs in deadline margins.",
                  "sourceIds": [
                    "v11a-schedule",
                    "v11a-mutex"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "a309-v11-24-k2",
                  "title": "計時器精度的驗證設計",
                  "titleEn": "Timer resolution validation design",
                  "text": "比較 tick 與高解析計時。 保留基準與擾動的完整輸入／輸出，以語義、容量或時間條件檢查，並明列假想模型未涵蓋的現實因素。",
                  "textEn": "Compare tick and high-resolution timing. Retain complete inputs/outputs for baseline and perturbation, check semantic/capacity/timing criteria and state real-world factors omitted from the hypothetical model.",
                  "sourceIds": [
                    "v11a-schedule",
                    "v11a-mutex"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "quiz": {
                "question": "本步審查「計時器精度」與整體「嵌入式即時作業系統」時，哪項陳述或驗證有依據？",
                "questionEn": "When reviewing timer resolution within embedded real-time operating systems, which statement or check is supported?",
                "options": [
                  "優先權繼承能消除所有阻塞時間。",
                  "平均延遲合格即證明硬即時合格。",
                  "比較 tick 與高解析計時。"
                ],
                "optionsEn": [
                  "Priority inheritance removes every blocking interval.",
                  "Passing mean latency proves hard real-time compliance.",
                  "Compare tick and high-resolution timing."
                ],
                "answer": 2,
                "explanation": "時鐘量化誤差需列入 deadline 裕量。 比較 tick 與高解析計時。 其餘選項混淆不同架構或證據的適用邊界。",
                "explanationEn": "Clock quantization belongs in deadline margins. Compare tick and high-resolution timing. The alternatives confuse architectural or evidence boundaries."
              }
