              "instructionEn": "Watch the mentor and identify data, control and timing relationships for boot abi. Contracts define entry registers and MMU state. Draw components/data flows offline; specify inputs, outputs, retained state and legal transitions. Build baseline and perturbed hypothetical cases and make a falsifiable prediction. Plan validation using: Audit a modeled bootloader handoff. Record versions, units, unknowns and out-of-model behavior.",
              "observation": "核對假想 bootloader 交接表。",
              "observationEn": "Audit a modeled bootloader handoff.",
              "failure": "常見誤判：一次成功啟動證明所有核心配置都正確。 本步需分開功能正確、資源上界與證據範圍，不可把假想結果當作真實平臺保證。",
              "failureEn": "Common mistake: One successful boot proves every kernel configuration. Separate correctness, resource bounds and evidence scope; hypothetical results are not real-platform guarantees.",
              "check": "提交「啟動 ABI」的兩情境架構／狀態圖、參數表與可反駁預測；標出哪些資料支援「入口暫存器與 MMU 狀態由契約定義。」。",
              "checkEn": "Submit boot abi two-case architecture/state diagrams, parameter table and falsifiable prediction; identify evidence supporting the principle.",
              "knowledge": [
                {
                  "id": "a311-v11-07-k1",
                  "title": "啟動 ABI的原理與邊界",
                  "titleEn": "Boot ABI principle and boundaries",
                  "text": "入口暫存器與 MMU 狀態由契約定義。",
                  "textEn": "Contracts define entry registers and MMU state.",
                  "sourceIds": [
