              "objectiveEn": "Establish reviewable architecture, principles and evidence for clock sources.",
              "instruction": "先觀看師傅示意，辨識「時鐘來源」的資料、控制與時間關係。計時來源會影響排程與延遲量測。 在離線工作臺畫出元件／資料流，列出輸入、輸出、保存狀態與合法轉移；建立基準與擾動兩種假想情境，寫下可被反駁的預測。以「核對假想頻率與換算。」設計下一步驗證。記錄版本、單位、未知參數與模型外的行為。",
              "instructionEn": "Watch the mentor and identify data, control and timing relationships for clock sources. Time sources affect scheduling and latency measures. Draw components/data flows offline; specify inputs, outputs, retained state and legal transitions. Build baseline and perturbed hypothetical cases and make a falsifiable prediction. Plan validation using: Check assumed frequency conversions. Record versions, units, unknowns and out-of-model behavior.",
              "observation": "核對假想頻率與換算。",
              "observationEn": "Check assumed frequency conversions.",
              "failure": "常見誤判：裝置樹本身會實作全部裝置驅動。 本步需分開功能正確、資源上界與證據範圍，不可把假想結果當作真實平臺保證。",
              "failureEn": "Common mistake: The devicetree itself implements all device drivers. Separate correctness, resource bounds and evidence scope; hypothetical results are not real-platform guarantees.",
              "check": "提交「時鐘來源」的兩情境架構／狀態圖、參數表與可反駁預測；標出哪些資料支援「計時來源會影響排程與延遲量測。」。",
              "checkEn": "Submit clock sources two-case architecture/state diagrams, parameter table and falsifiable prediction; identify evidence supporting the principle.",
              "knowledge": [
                {
                  "id": "a311-v11-17-k1",
                  "title": "時鐘來源的原理與邊界",
                  "titleEn": "Clock sources principle and boundaries",
                  "text": "計時來源會影響排程與延遲量測。",
                  "textEn": "Time sources affect scheduling and latency measures.",
