              "objective": "以「排程預算」建立可檢查的架構、原理與驗證依據。",
              "objectiveEn": "Establish reviewable architecture, principles and evidence for scheduling budgets.",
              "instruction": "先觀看師傅示意，辨識「排程預算」的資料、控制與時間關係。隔離記憶體不能自行隔離 CPU 時間。 在離線工作臺畫出元件／資料流，列出輸入、輸出、保存狀態與合法轉移；建立基準與擾動兩種假想情境，寫下可被反駁的預測。以「比較失控服務的時間佔用。」設計下一步驗證。記錄版本、單位、未知參數與模型外的行為。",
              "instructionEn": "Watch the mentor and identify data, control and timing relationships for scheduling budgets. Memory isolation alone does not isolate CPU time. Draw components/data flows offline; specify inputs, outputs, retained state and legal transitions. Build baseline and perturbed hypothetical cases and make a falsifiable prediction. Plan validation using: Compare CPU use by an unbounded service. Record versions, units, unknowns and out-of-model behavior.",
              "observation": "比較失控服務的時間佔用。",
              "observationEn": "Compare CPU use by an unbounded service.",
              "failure": "常見誤判：使用者態驅動無需考慮 DMA 權限。 本步需分開功能正確、資源上界與證據範圍，不可把假想結果當作真實平臺保證。",
              "failureEn": "Common mistake: User-mode drivers need no DMA permission analysis. Separate correctness, resource bounds and evidence scope; hypothetical results are not real-platform guarantees.",
              "check": "提交「排程預算」的兩情境架構／狀態圖、參數表與可反駁預測；標出哪些資料支援「隔離記憶體不能自行隔離 CPU 時間。」。",
              "checkEn": "Submit scheduling budgets two-case architecture/state diagrams, parameter table and falsifiable prediction; identify evidence supporting the principle.",
              "knowledge": [
                {
                  "id": "a312-v11-23-k1",
                  "title": "排程預算的原理與邊界",
                  "titleEn": "Scheduling budgets principle and boundaries",
                  "text": "隔離記憶體不能自行隔離 CPU 時間。",
                  "textEn": "Memory isolation alone does not isolate CPU time.",
                  "sourceIds": [
                    "v11a-ipc",
                    "v11a-proof"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "a312-v11-23-k2",
                  "title": "排程預算的驗證設計",
                  "titleEn": "Scheduling budgets validation design",
                  "text": "比較失控服務的時間佔用。 保留基準與擾動的完整輸入／輸出，以語義、容量或時間條件檢查，並明列假想模型未涵蓋的現實因素。",
                  "textEn": "Compare CPU use by an unbounded service. Retain complete inputs/outputs for baseline and perturbation, check semantic/capacity/timing criteria and state real-world factors omitted from the hypothetical model.",
                  "sourceIds": [
                    "v11a-ipc",
                    "v11a-proof"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "quiz": {
                "question": "本步審查「排程預算」與整體「微核心作業系統架構」時，哪項陳述或驗證有依據？",
                "questionEn": "When reviewing scheduling budgets within microkernel operating-system architecture, which statement or check is supported?",
                "options": [
                  "核心證明自動涵蓋所有驅動與應用。",
                  "隔離記憶體不能自行隔離 CPU 時間。",
                  "使用者態驅動無需考慮 DMA 權限。"
                ],
                "optionsEn": [
                  "Kernel proofs automatically cover all drivers and applications.",
                  "Memory isolation alone does not isolate CPU time.",
                  "User-mode drivers need no DMA permission analysis."
                ],
                "answer": 1,
                "explanation": "隔離記憶體不能自行隔離 CPU 時間。 比較失控服務的時間佔用。 其餘選項混淆不同架構或證據的適用邊界。",
                "explanationEn": "Memory isolation alone does not isolate CPU time. Compare CPU use by an unbounded service. The alternatives confuse architectural or evidence boundaries."
              }
