              "title": "Group commit：原理與架構",
              "titleEn": "Group commit: principles and architecture",
              "objective": "以「Group commit」建立可檢查的架構、原理與驗證依據。",
              "objectiveEn": "Establish reviewable architecture, principles and evidence for group commit.",
              "instruction": "先觀看師傅示意，辨識「Group commit」的資料、控制與時間關係。共用 flush 改變吞吐與等待分佈。 在離線工作臺畫出元件／資料流，列出輸入、輸出、保存狀態與合法轉移；建立基準與擾動兩種假想情境，寫下可被反駁的預測。以「核算本課批次提交上界。」設計下一步驗證。記錄版本、單位、未知參數與模型外的行為。",
              "instructionEn": "Watch the mentor and identify data, control and timing relationships for group commit. Shared flush changes throughput and waiting. Draw components/data flows offline; specify inputs, outputs, retained state and legal transitions. Build baseline and perturbed hypothetical cases and make a falsifiable prediction. Plan validation using: Audit group-commit throughput bounds. Record versions, units, unknowns and out-of-model behavior.",
              "observation": "核算本課批次提交上界。",
              "observationEn": "Audit group-commit throughput bounds.",
              "failure": "常見誤判：MVCC 等於所有交易均為 serializable。 本步需分開功能正確、資源上界與證據範圍，不可把假想結果當作真實平臺保證。",
              "failureEn": "Common mistake: MVCC makes every transaction serializable. Separate correctness, resource bounds and evidence scope; hypothetical results are not real-platform guarantees.",
              "check": "提交「Group commit」的兩情境架構／狀態圖、參數表與可反駁預測；標出哪些資料支援「共用 flush 改變吞吐與等待分佈。」。",
              "checkEn": "Submit group commit two-case architecture/state diagrams, parameter table and falsifiable prediction; identify evidence supporting the principle.",
              "knowledge": [
                {
                  "id": "a318-v11-21-k1",
                  "title": "Group commit的原理與邊界",
                  "titleEn": "Group commit principle and boundaries",
                  "text": "共用 flush 改變吞吐與等待分佈。",
                  "textEn": "Shared flush changes throughput and waiting.",
                  "sourceIds": [
                    "v11a-wal",
                    "v11a-isolation"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "a318-v11-21-k2",
                  "title": "Group commit的驗證設計",
                  "titleEn": "Group commit validation design",
                  "text": "核算本課批次提交上界。 保留基準與擾動的完整輸入／輸出，以語義、容量或時間條件檢查，並明列假想模型未涵蓋的現實因素。",
                  "textEn": "Audit group-commit throughput bounds. Retain complete inputs/outputs for baseline and perturbation, check semantic/capacity/timing criteria and state real-world factors omitted from the hypothetical model.",
                  "sourceIds": [
                    "v11a-wal",
                    "v11a-isolation"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "quiz": {
                "question": "本步審查「Group commit」與整體「資料庫交易與日誌」時，哪項陳述或驗證有依據？",
                "questionEn": "When reviewing group commit within database transactions and logging, which statement or check is supported?",
                "options": [
                  "MVCC 等於所有交易均為 serializable。",
                  "資料頁先耐久而日誌後寫仍符合 WAL。",
                  "共用 flush 改變吞吐與等待分佈。"
                ],
                "optionsEn": [
                  "MVCC makes every transaction serializable.",
                  "Durable pages before their logs satisfy WAL.",
                  "Shared flush changes throughput and waiting."
                ],
                "answer": 2,
                "explanation": "共用 flush 改變吞吐與等待分佈。 核算本課批次提交上界。 其餘選項混淆不同架構或證據的適用邊界。",
                "explanationEn": "Shared flush changes throughput and waiting. Audit group-commit throughput bounds. The alternatives confuse architectural or evidence boundaries."
              }
