                  "titleEn": "Failure model validation design",
                  "text": "列出模型內與外的失效。 保留基準與擾動的完整輸入／輸出，以語義、容量或時間條件檢查，並明列假想模型未涵蓋的現實因素。",
                  "textEn": "List in-model and out-of-model failures. Retain complete inputs/outputs for baseline and perturbation, check semantic/capacity/timing criteria and state real-world factors omitted from the hypothetical model.",
                  "sourceIds": [
                    "v11a-raft",
                    "v11a-etcd"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "a319-v11-02-k3",
                  "title": "本課原創量化算例",
                  "titleEn": "Original course worked example",
                  "text": "假設五個投票節點，多數=3，最多容忍兩個節點不可用；3+2 分割僅 3 節點側可在其他條件滿足時提交。30 ms 對等 RTT 只提供路徑預算，不保證 30 ms 提交，仍需持久化與排程。",
                  "textEn": "With five voting nodes, majority=3 and at most two unavailable nodes are tolerated. In a 3+2 split only the three-node side may commit if other conditions hold. A 30 ms peer RTT is a path budget, not a commit guarantee.",
                  "sourceIds": [
                    "v11a-raft",
                    "v11a-etcd"
                  ],
                  "authorship": "original-hypothetical-exercise"
                }
              ],
              "quiz": {
                "question": "本步審查「失效模型」與整體「分散式共識服務」時，哪項陳述或驗證有依據？",
                "questionEn": "When reviewing failure model within distributed consensus services, which statement or check is supported?",
                "options": [
                  "五節點 Raft 兩節點仍可單獨提交。",
                  "列出模型內與外的失效。",
                  "Raft 的 crash 模型自動防止 Byzantine 節點。"
                ],
                "optionsEn": [
                  "Two nodes alone can commit in five-node Raft.",
                  "List in-model and out-of-model failures.",
                  "Raft crash tolerance automatically prevents Byzantine nodes."
                ],
                "answer": 1,
                "explanation": "Raft 一般處理 crash fault 而非任意惡意節點。 列出模型內與外的失效。 其餘選項混淆不同架構或證據的適用邊界。",
                "explanationEn": "Raft generally handles crashes, not arbitrary malicious nodes. List in-model and out-of-model failures. The alternatives confuse architectural or evidence boundaries."
              }
            },
