              "title": "事件時間：原理與架構",
              "titleEn": "Event time: principles and architecture",
              "objective": "以「事件時間」建立可檢查的架構、原理與驗證依據。",
              "objectiveEn": "Establish reviewable architecture, principles and evidence for event time.",
              "instruction": "先觀看師傅示意，辨識「事件時間」的資料、控制與時間關係。事件發生時間不同於處理到達時間。 在離線工作臺畫出元件／資料流，列出輸入、輸出、保存狀態與合法轉移；建立基準與擾動兩種假想情境，寫下可被反駁的預測。以「將相同事件以兩順序送入模型。」設計下一步驗證。記錄版本、單位、未知參數與模型外的行為。",
              "instructionEn": "Watch the mentor and identify data, control and timing relationships for event time. Event time differs from processing arrival time. Draw components/data flows offline; specify inputs, outputs, retained state and legal transitions. Build baseline and perturbed hypothetical cases and make a falsifiable prediction. Plan validation using: Model two arrival orders of the same events. Record versions, units, unknowns and out-of-model behavior.",
              "observation": "將相同事件以兩順序送入模型。",
              "observationEn": "Model two arrival orders of the same events.",
              "failure": "常見誤判：所有分區 offset 能建立全域事件時間。 本步需分開功能正確、資源上界與證據範圍，不可把假想結果當作真實平臺保證。",
              "failureEn": "Common mistake: Offsets across partitions establish global event time. Separate correctness, resource bounds and evidence scope; hypothetical results are not real-platform guarantees.",
              "check": "提交「事件時間」的兩情境架構／狀態圖、參數表與可反駁預測；標出哪些資料支援「事件發生時間不同於處理到達時間。」。",
              "checkEn": "Submit event time two-case architecture/state diagrams, parameter table and falsifiable prediction; identify evidence supporting the principle.",
              "knowledge": [
                {
                  "id": "a320-v11-09-k1",
                  "title": "事件時間的原理與邊界",
                  "titleEn": "Event time principle and boundaries",
                  "text": "事件發生時間不同於處理到達時間。",
                  "textEn": "Event time differs from processing arrival time.",
                  "sourceIds": [
