              "title": "宣告狀態：原理與架構",
              "titleEn": "Desired state: principles and architecture",
              "objective": "以「宣告狀態」建立可檢查的架構、原理與驗證依據。",
              "objectiveEn": "Establish reviewable architecture, principles and evidence for desired state.",
              "instruction": "先觀看師傅示意，辨識「宣告狀態」的資料、控制與時間關係。宣告期望與實際狀態會短暫不同。 在離線工作臺畫出元件／資料流，列出輸入、輸出、保存狀態與合法轉移；建立基準與擾動兩種假想情境，寫下可被反駁的預測。以「畫 reconcile 的迭代。」設計下一步驗證。記錄版本、單位、未知參數與模型外的行為。",
              "instructionEn": "Watch the mentor and identify data, control and timing relationships for desired state. Desired and observed state may temporarily differ. Draw components/data flows offline; specify inputs, outputs, retained state and legal transitions. Build baseline and perturbed hypothetical cases and make a falsifiable prediction. Plan validation using: Draw reconciliation iterations. Record versions, units, unknowns and out-of-model behavior.",
              "observation": "畫 reconcile 的迭代。",
              "observationEn": "Draw reconciliation iterations.",
              "failure": "常見誤判：所有 running pod 都已可對使用者提供服務。 本步需分開功能正確、資源上界與證據範圍，不可把假想結果當作真實平臺保證。",
              "failureEn": "Common mistake: Every running pod is ready for users. Separate correctness, resource bounds and evidence scope; hypothetical results are not real-platform guarantees.",
              "check": "提交「宣告狀態」的兩情境架構／狀態圖、參數表與可反駁預測；標出哪些資料支援「宣告期望與實際狀態會短暫不同。」。",
              "checkEn": "Submit desired state two-case architecture/state diagrams, parameter table and falsifiable prediction; identify evidence supporting the principle.",
              "knowledge": [
                {
                  "id": "a321-v11-01-k1",
                  "title": "宣告狀態的原理與邊界",
                  "titleEn": "Desired state principle and boundaries",
                  "text": "宣告期望與實際狀態會短暫不同。",
                  "textEn": "Desired and observed state may temporarily differ.",
                  "sourceIds": [
                    "v11a-k8s",
                    "v11a-pod"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "a321-v11-01-k2",
                  "title": "宣告狀態的驗證設計",
                  "titleEn": "Desired state validation design",
                  "text": "畫 reconcile 的迭代。 保留基準與擾動的完整輸入／輸出，以語義、容量或時間條件檢查，並明列假想模型未涵蓋的現實因素。",
                  "textEn": "Draw reconciliation iterations. Retain complete inputs/outputs for baseline and perturbation, check semantic/capacity/timing criteria and state real-world factors omitted from the hypothetical model.",
                  "sourceIds": [
                    "v11a-k8s",
                    "v11a-pod"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "a321-v11-01-k3",
                  "title": "本課原創量化算例",
                  "titleEn": "Original course worked example",
                  "text": "假設四節點各 8 CPU，每節點保留 1 CPU，allocatable 合計 28 CPU。每個不可跨節點拆分的 pod request 2 CPU，單節點只能放 floor(7/2)=3 個，四節點最多 12 個；14 個 pod 雖需合計 28 CPU，仍確定無法全部排程。拓撲、記憶體與裝置限制可能使上限更低。",
                  "textEn": "Four assumed 8-CPU nodes reserve 1 CPU each, totaling 28 allocatable CPUs. Each indivisible 2-CPU-request pod fits on one node: floor(7/2)=3 pods/node and at most 12 across four nodes. Fourteen pods need 28 CPU in aggregate but definitely cannot all schedule; topology, memory or device constraints may lower the bound further.",
                  "sourceIds": [
                    "v11a-k8s",
                    "v11a-pod"
                  ],
                  "authorship": "original-hypothetical-exercise"
                }
              ],
              "quiz": {
                "question": "本步審查「宣告狀態」與整體「容器編排叢集」時，哪項陳述或驗證有依據？",
                "questionEn": "When reviewing desired state within container-orchestration clusters, which statement or check is supported?",
                "options": [
                  "宣告期望與實際狀態會短暫不同。",
                  "所有 running pod 都已可對使用者提供服務。",
                  "CPU 總量吻合就能忽略 affinity 排程。"
                ],
                "optionsEn": [
                  "Desired and observed state may temporarily differ.",
                  "Every running pod is ready for users.",
                  "Matching CPU totals permits ignoring affinity."
                ],
                "answer": 0,
                "explanation": "宣告期望與實際狀態會短暫不同。 畫 reconcile 的迭代。 其餘選項混淆不同架構或證據的適用邊界。",
                "explanationEn": "Desired and observed state may temporarily differ. Draw reconciliation iterations. The alternatives confuse architectural or evidence boundaries."
              }
            },
